
>> {"method":"initialize","params":{"clientInfo":{"version":"1","name":"rc2-acer-test"},"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{}},"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0"}
<< {"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"capabilities":{"resources":{"listChanged":false,"subscribe":false},"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"instructions":"JETCARP runs cellular automata (the Game of Life and many other rules) on square, hexagon, triangle, Archimedean, k-uniform and aperiodic (Spectre, hat, Penrose) tilings, and keeps a library of the patterns its searches find. Typical flow: world_new (a tiling and rules) -> world_edit (draw or paste) -> world_step -> world_read / world_render. Long searches: search_start, job_status, then library_query for the finds. Call help for worked examples, reference for rule names, tilings, palettes and seeds. The JETCARP book is available as resources (jetcarp://docs/...) and through help {\"page\": ...}.","protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","resultType":"complete","serverInfo":{"name":"jetcarp","title":"JETCARP cellular automata","version":"0.4.2-rc.2"}}}
>> {"method":"notifications/initialized","jsonrpc":"2.0"}
>> {"method":"tools/list","params":{},"id":2,"jsonrpc":"2.0"}
<< {"id":2,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"cacheScope":"public","resultType":"complete","tools":[{"annotations":{"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Start here if you are new to JETCARP. Explains what JETCARP is and how these tools fit together, with worked examples you can copy. `topic`: \"overview\" (default: concepts, coordinates, a glider in Life, Brian's Brain, a rule on hexagons, a sandpile), \"world\" (drawing, pasting, reseeding, commands, objects), \"library\" (finding, reading and curating patterns, ant runs and Quick Start entries), \"searches\" (long searches as background jobs: start, wait, read the finds, stop, resume), \"scripts\" (every run_script function), \"packs\" (checking, importing and publishing packs), \"setup\" (this installation as its user set it up: profile, folders, packs, GPU, library; read only, since setup is the user's choice) or \"pages\" (the pages of the JETCARP book). `page` returns one book page as Markdown, e.g. {\"page\": \"guides/searching\"} (the resources jetcarp://docs/{page}). `schema` returns the settings of a tool argument that names a jetcarp://schema/ resource, e.g. {\"schema\": \"search_start/hunt\"}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"page":{"description":"A page of the JETCARP book by its path without .md, e.g. \"guides/searching\" (topic pages lists them).","type":"string"},"schema":{"description":"A JSON Schema: a tool argument's settings (\"search_start/hunt\" is jetcarp://schema/search_start/hunt), \"scene.json\" or \"pack.json\".","type":"string"},"topic":{"description":"Which guide (default overview).","enum":["overview","world","library","searches","scripts","packs","setup","pages"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"help","title":"JETCARP help and worked examples"},{"annotations":{"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Lists what there is to choose from. `what`: \"rules\" (default: the named rules with notation, family and a line each, and how rule notation works; any name or notation works as a CA's `rule`, e.g. \"Life\", \"B36/S23\", \"Brian's Brain\", \"W30\", \"Ant RL\"), \"tilings\" (tiling ids for world_new and their neighbour counts; with `search`, catalog tilings such as \"k2-005\" or \"3.4.6.4\"), \"isohedral\" (Kaplan's 81 isohedral tile types), \"palettes\" (built-in palettes and their colours), \"seeds\" (the forms a CA's `seed` takes), or \"commands\" (the command objects world_edit's `commands` applies). Examples: {\"what\": \"rules\", \"family\": \"Generations\"}, {\"what\": \"tilings\", \"search\": \"k2-\"}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"family":{"description":"rules: only this family (part of its name, any case), e.g. \"Life-like\", \"Generations\", \"Agents\".","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"tilings: With `search`: most matches listed (default 60).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"search":{"description":"tilings: List the tilings (families, catalog tilings, isohedral types) whose id or name contains this text, any case, e.g. \"k2-\", \"3.4.6.4\", \"ih4\". Default: the tiling families.","type":"string"},"what":{"description":"What to list (default rules).","enum":["rules","tilings","isohedral","palettes","seeds","commands"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"reference","title":"Rules, tilings, palettes, seeds, commands"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Replaces the current world. Build one from a tiling (the grid of cells) and the CAs (cellular automata) that run on it: {\"tiling\": \"hex\", \"width\": 60, \"height\": 60, \"boundary\": \"wrap\", \"cas\": [\"B24/S35\"]}. Each CA starts from its rule's default seed (a random soup for Life-like rules) unless given one: {\"cas\": [{\"rule\": \"Life\", \"seed\": \"empty\"}]} is a blank field to draw on (reference {\"what\": \"seeds\"} lists the seeds, {\"what\": \"tilings\"} the tilings). Size: width and height (8 to 4096 unit cells each), or `cells` (about that many, up to 4000000), or `level` on aperiodic tilings. Or open one: `quickstart` (a Quick Start entry by handle, e.g. \"life\"), `pattern` (a library pattern on a grid sized for it, e.g. \"glider\"), `scene` (scene JSON, as world_status {\"scene\": true} returns it) or `path` (a scene file). Returns the world's status with each CA's id. Next: world_edit, world_step, world_read, world_render.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"boundary":{"description":"\"wrap\" (default), \"dead\", or \"live\" (aperiodic tilings are always dead).","type":"string"},"cas":{"description":"The CAs, in order: rule names or notation (\"Life\", \"B3/S23\"), or CA objects as in a scene ({\"rule\": \"Life\", \"seed\": \"random:0.2\"}); one string is one CA."},"cells":{"description":"Instead of width and height: about this many cells in a roughly square region.","type":"integer"},"height":{"description":"Grid height in unit cells.","type":"integer"},"level":{"description":"Aperiodic tilings: the substitution level.","type":"integer"},"name":{"description":"Scene name.","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"A scene .json file.","type":"string"},"pattern":{"description":"A library pattern (id, prefix or name, e.g. `glider`) alone on a wrapped grid sized for it, in a rule it runs in.","type":"string"},"quickstart":{"description":"A Quick Start entry by handle (`life`, `find:<id>`, `atlas:<...>`, `qs-<hex>`): the scene the app's Quick Start opens.","type":"string"},"rng_seed":{"description":"Random seed (default 1): the same seed gives the same run. Any `u64`; beyond 2^53 - 1 also as a string of decimal digits.","minimum":0,"pattern":"^[0-9]+$","type":["integer","string"]},"scene":{"description":"Scene JSON: the object, or its text."},"tiling":{"description":"Tiling id (reference {\"what\": \"tilings\"}): \"square\" (default), \"hex\", \"triangle\", \"cairo\", \"spectre\" (aperiodic), a vertex configuration such as \"3.4.6.4\", or a catalog id such as \"k2-005\".","type":"string"},"tiling_params":{"description":"Advanced: tile shape parameters (JETCARP tile JSON `params`)."},"width":{"description":"Grid width in unit cells (with height).","type":"integer"}},"type":"object"},"name":"world_new","title":"Make or open a world"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Reports the current world: tiling and grid size (width x height for coordinates), generation, state hash, whether it is running, empty, frozen, or repeating with a period (checked exactly), population per field, and the CAs with their ids and rules. Cheap; call it whenever you need ids or sizes. {\"scene\": true} returns the world's scene JSON instead (world_new {\"scene\": ...} reproduces this exact state); {\"save_path\": \"glider.json\"} also writes it to a file (the app and `jetcarp run` open it).","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"save_path":{"description":"The .json file to write (its folder is created).","type":"string"},"scene":{"default":false,"description":"Also return the scene: tiling, CAs, random seed, and the command log since the last reset (opening it reproduces this exact state).","type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"},"name":"world_status","title":"World status"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Looks at a CA's field. With no arguments: a text picture of the smallest box around the non-empty cells (one row per line, prefixed by its row number y, with a ruler of column numbers; '.' empty, 'O' live, digits for higher states or sandpile grains), the live-cell count and the bounding box. x, y, width, height show a fixed region; {\"format\": \"list\"} gives [x, y, state] triples instead. {\"format\": \"objects\"} runs the object finder: every still life, oscillator, spaceship and gun in the field, named and classed, with where it is (`catalog`: true also stores each distinct one in the library). {\"cell\": {\"x\": 3, \"y\": 4}} describes one cell: its tile type, centre, value in every field, and its neighbours in clockwise order (the neighbour layout on hexagons, triangles and other tilings, before you draw).","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ca":{"description":"Which CA: its id number or its name (world_status lists them). Default: the first CA.","type":["integer","string"]},"catalog":{"default":false,"description":"With format objects: Also verify each distinct still life, oscillator and spaceship and add it to the library (copies add to its seen count), as a search would.","type":"boolean"},"cell":{"description":"One cell to describe instead: {\"x\", \"y\"} or {\"index\"}. Settings: jetcarp://schema/world_read/cell","type":"object"},"format":{"description":"\"picture\" (default), \"list\" of non-empty cells as [x, y, state], or \"objects\" (the object finder).","enum":["picture","list","objects"],"type":"string"},"height":{"description":"Region height (default 40 with x, y; at most 200).","type":"integer"},"max_period":{"description":"With format objects: Longest period looked for (default 64, at most 1024).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"width":{"description":"Region width (default 40 with x, y; at most 200).","type":"integer"},"x":{"description":"Left column of the region (default: the box around every non-empty cell).","type":"integer"},"y":{"description":"Top row of the region.","type":"integer"}},"type":"object"},"name":"world_read","title":"Read cells, a cell, or the objects"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Changes the world through logged commands (world_status {\"scene\": true} replays them). Give one of: `cells` to draw a text picture, RLE, [x, y] cells or cell indices, e.g. {\"cells\": {\"pattern\": \".O.\\n..O\\nOOO\", \"x\": 10, \"y\": 10}} (a glider moving down-right; x = column, y = row, (0, 0) is the top-left cell); `paste` to place a library pattern, e.g. {\"paste\": {\"id\": \"glider\", \"x\": 10, \"y\": 10, \"orientation\": 1}}; `reseed` to put new life into a settled world, now ({\"reseed\": {\"mode\": \"blobs\"}}) or by policies; or `commands`, the app's own commands in order, e.g. {\"commands\": [{\"op\": \"add_ca\", \"ca\": {\"rule\": \"Ant RL\", \"seed\": \"ants:3\"}}]}; reference {\"what\": \"commands\"} lists them. `ca` picks the CA (id or name; default the first) for cells, paste and reseed. Next: world_step, world_read.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ca":{"description":"Which CA: its id number or its name (world_status lists them). Default: the first CA.","type":["integer","string"]},"cells":{"description":"Cells to draw into a CA's field: one of `pattern`, `rle`, `cells` or `indices` (or only `clear_first`). Settings: jetcarp://schema/world_edit/cells","type":"object"},"commands":{"description":"Command objects, each with an \"op\" field (one object, or their JSON text, works too): add_ca, remove_ca, update_ca, seed, clear, set_cells, step, reset, set_rng_state, set_tiling, sandpile, set_palette, reseed, set_reseed, ...","items":{"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"paste":{"description":"A library pattern to paste, and where. Needs `id`. Settings: jetcarp://schema/world_edit/paste","type":"object"},"reseed":{"description":"Reseed now, set the automatic policies, or report them. Settings: jetcarp://schema/world_edit/reseed","type":"object"}},"type":"object"},"name":"world_edit","title":"Draw, paste, reseed, or apply commands"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Advances the world by `generations` (default 1; at most 1,000,000 per call, and at most 2 billion cell updates, cells x generations); every enabled CA steps together. Returns the new generation, populations and status (running, empty, frozen, or repeating with its period). {\"stop_when_settled\": true} stops as soon as the world is empty, frozen or exactly periodic (up to 5000 generations when no count is given). Stops early when the client cancels the call.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"generations":{"description":"Generations to run (default 1, or up to 5000 with `stop_when_settled`).","type":"integer"},"stop_when_settled":{"default":false,"description":"Stop as soon as the world is empty, frozen, or exactly periodic.","type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"},"name":"world_step","title":"Run generations"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Renders the whole world as a PNG and returns it, so you can see it: empty cells dark, live cells in the CA's palette, brighter for young cells. The user sees it only where the client shows tool images (terminal clients don't), so pass `save_path` when they want the picture: it also writes the PNG (scene embedded) and says where. {\"wallpaper\": {\"size\": \"4K\"}} writes desktop-sized pictures instead and returns their paths (also on a fresh grid sized for the picture, or one picture per monitor, cut so they line up).","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"max_side":{"description":"Longest image side in pixels, 64 to 2048 (default 640).","type":"integer"},"outlines":{"description":"Draw tile outlines (default: only when tiles are at least 7 px).","type":"boolean"},"save_path":{"description":"Also write the PNG to this file (scene embedded; its folder is created).","type":"string"},"wallpaper":{"description":"Write desktop-sized pictures of the world instead. Settings: jetcarp://schema/world_render/wallpaper","type":"object"}},"type":"object"},"name":"world_render","title":"Render a picture"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Runs a JETCARP script (the Rhai language) and returns its log, errors with line numbers, output folders and sweep summaries. Scripts make their own worlds (the current world is not changed), run them until something happens, save PNGs, and run parallel rule sweeps into new folders under the output folder. Example: `let w = world(#{ tiling: \"hex\", size: [120, 80], boundary: \"dead\" }); w.add_ca(\"HexW3 8229\", #{ seed: \"top_center\" }); let r = w.run(#{ until: \"done\" }); print(r.generations); w.save_png(out_dir(\"test\") + \"/a.png\");` or `sweep(#{ rules: \"W\", until: \"done\", png: #{ size: [400, 300] } });`. help {\"topic\": \"scripts\"} lists every function. Limits: 600 seconds at most (default 60, `max_seconds`), worlds of at most 4000000 cells; files are written only inside the output folder and read only there. Stops early when the client cancels the call.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cell_px":{"description":"Tile size in pixels for screen-sized worlds (default 8).","maximum":256,"minimum":1,"type":"number"},"check_only":{"description":"Only check the script for syntax errors.","type":"boolean"},"log_lines":{"description":"Most log lines to return, the last ones (default 200).","maximum":2000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"max_seconds":{"description":"Stop the script after this many seconds (default 60).","maximum":600.0,"minimum":1,"type":"number"},"params":{"description":"Values the script reads as `params.key`.","type":"object"},"screen":{"description":"Screen size for size: \"screen\" worlds and the default image size, e.g. \"1920x1080\" (default).","type":"string"},"script":{"description":"The script text (Rhai).","type":"string"}},"required":["script"],"type":"object"},"name":"run_script","title":"Run a JETCARP script"},{"annotations":{"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Lists or reads the library: what searches found and what you and the user kept. `kind`: \"pattern\" (default: verified still lifes, oscillators, spaceships, guns, puffers and movers, each with the rules it was verified in and the range of rules it runs identically in), \"ant\" (ant and turmite runs, classed highway, periodic, symmetric, bounded or chaotic), \"quickstart\" (the app's Quick Start entries: built-in examples, packs, explore atlases, promotions) or \"summary\" (counts). Listings come best first (`limit`, default 20, at most 100; `offset` pages); each filter says which kind it applies to. With `id`, one record in full: a pattern's rules, sightings, the cells of its phases as text, and which way it moves per paste orientation; an ant run's outcome and proof; a Quick Start entry with its scene. Examples: {\"class\": \"spaceship\", \"tiling\": \"hex\"}, {\"works_in\": \"B36/S23\"}, {\"kind\": \"ant\", \"outcome\": \"highway\"}, {\"id\": \"glider\", \"phases\": 4}. Next: world_new {\"pattern\": id} or world_edit {\"paste\": {\"id\": id}} to run one; library_curate to curate; media_render for pictures.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"class":{"description":"Patterns of this class: still_life, oscillator, spaceship, puffer, gun, mover.","type":"string"},"discovered_by":{"description":"Patterns found by: search, script, llm, user.","type":"string"},"hidden":{"description":"Quick Start: Only hidden entries (true) or only shown ones (false); default both.","type":"boolean"},"id":{"description":"Read this record in full instead: a pattern's id, prefix or name (\"glider\"), an ant run (ant-...) or a Quick Start handle (find:..., life).","type":"string"},"job":{"description":"Ants of this search job.","type":"integer"},"kind":{"description":"What to list or read (default pattern; with `id`, the id's form says).","enum":["pattern","ant","quickstart","summary"],"type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"At most this many records (default 20, at most 100).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"max_period":{"description":"Patterns with a period of at most this.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"min_period":{"description":"Patterns with a period of at least this.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"min_score":{"description":"Patterns scoring at least this (0-100).","type":"number"},"neighborhood":{"description":"Patterns with this neighbourhood: `touch` or `edge`.","type":"string"},"offset":{"description":"Skip this many patterns first (paging).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"order":{"description":"Pattern order: score (default), seen, rare, newest, updated, cells, period, rating, id.","type":"string"},"outcome":{"description":"Ants with this outcome: highway, periodic, symmetric, bounded, chaotic.","type":"string"},"phases":{"description":"Phases to draw as text (default 1).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"rule":{"description":"Patterns verified in a rule whose notation contains this; ants: this turn string or table (`RL`, `Turmite LLRR`; its mirror image matches too).","type":"string"},"sort":{"description":"Ant order: score (default), onset, period, speed, rule.","type":"string"},"source":{"description":"Quick Start: only entries from this source: builtin, pack, atlas, promotion, or all (default: all but builtin).","type":"string"},"state":{"description":"Patterns in this curation state: new, reviewed, promoted, rejected.","type":"string"},"tag":{"description":"Patterns with this tag.","type":"string"},"text":{"description":"Patterns whose name or label contains this; Quick Start entries whose title, rule or tiling contains it.","type":"string"},"tiling":{"description":"Tiling family id (`hex`), catalog id (`k2-001`), or part of the tiling name.","type":"string"},"works_in":{"description":"Patterns that run in this rule (inside their rule range, or verified there).","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"library_query","title":"List or read library records"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Changes the library. With `id` (a pattern's id, prefix or name; ant-...; or a Quick Start handle) give one of: `changes` (name, tags, notes, rating 1-5, state), e.g. {\"id\": \"glider\", \"changes\": {\"rating\": 4, \"append_notes\": \"LLM: a clean c/4 ship\"}} (mark text you wrote as yours); `hidden` (Quick Start entries: true leaves it out of the menu, packs and the website; false shows it again); or `remove`: true (deletes the record for good, a pattern with its rules, sightings and Quick Start entry; ask the user first). Without `id`: `quickstart` adds an entry to the app's Quick Start under \"My finds\", e.g. {\"quickstart\": {\"pattern\": \"<id>\", \"title\": \"Trihex glider\"}}; or `compounds` finds stored patterns that are really several independent objects (two gliders side by side) and lists their parts ({\"compounds\": {}}; with {\"apply\": true} it stores the parts instead).","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"changes":{"description":"Patterns and ant runs: the changes (what is not given stays). Settings: jetcarp://schema/library_curate/changes","type":"object"},"compounds":{"description":"Find stored patterns that are several independent objects, as a resumable job. Settings: jetcarp://schema/library_curate/compounds","type":"object"},"hidden":{"description":"Quick Start entries: leave it out of the menu, packs and the website (true), or show it again (false).","type":"boolean"},"id":{"description":"The record: a pattern's id, unique prefix or name; an ant run's id (ant-...); or a Quick Start entry's handle (find:..., atlas:..., life).","type":"string"},"kind":{"description":"What `id` names (default: from its form).","enum":["pattern","ant","quickstart"],"type":"string"},"quickstart":{"description":"Add an entry to the Quick Start under \"My finds\". Settings: jetcarp://schema/library_curate/quickstart","type":"object"},"remove":{"description":"Delete the record for good (true).","type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"},"name":"library_curate","title":"Curate library records"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Starts a search as a library job and returns its job id at once; job_status follows it, job_stop stops it. Give one strategy as a key holding its settings (every setting is optional; each strategy names the resource listing them): `hunt`, `search`, `ants`, `census`, `mover`, `pile`, `collide`, `evolve` or `explore` (help {\"topic\": \"searches\"} explains each). Or {\"resume\": job} carries on a stopped job. The job runs on a thread of this server, so it stops when the server exits (it stays resumable); {\"detach\": true} runs it in a process of its own that outlives the server (explore searches do this by default where they can). `wait_s` waits for the job to end, and `budget` ends this run early. Results go to the library (library_query), an explore search's runs to search_runs. Examples: {\"hunt\": {\"rules\": [\"B3/S23\"], \"soups\": 20000}, \"wait_s\": 120}, {\"ants\": {\"tilings\": \"hex\", \"strings\": [2, 4]}}, {\"pile\": {\"tiling\": \"hex\", \"grains\": \"1e6\"}}, {\"collide\": {\"a\": \"block\", \"b\": \"glider\"}, \"wait_s\": 60}, {\"explore\": {\"tilings\": \"square,hex\", \"families\": \"life_like,cyclic\"}, \"budget\": {\"minutes\": 5}}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ants":{"description":"Ant and turmite rules on a periodic tiling, every run classed and stored. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_start/ants","type":"object"},"budget":{"description":"This run's budget: `minutes`, `items` or `until`. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_start/budget","type":"object"},"census":{"description":"Rules classed by what their soups do (die, freeze, oscillate, grow, ...), with a table and a contact sheet. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_start/census","type":"object"},"collide":{"description":"Pattern `b` shot into pattern `a` at every offset and phase. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_start/collide","type":"object"},"detach":{"default":false,"description":"Run in a process of its own (`jetcarp jobs resume JOB`) and answer at once.","type":"boolean"},"evolve":{"description":"The evolutionary glider search, storing the movers it verifies. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_start/evolve","type":"object"},"explore":{"description":"The broad search over tilings, rule families, rules and seeds (search_runs reads its runs). Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_start/explore","type":"object"},"gpu":{"description":"Use the GPU (true) or only the CPU (false); results are identical. Default: the job's own choice, else JETCARP's GPU setting (automatic).","type":"boolean"},"hunt":{"description":"Small random soups on an unbounded plane, each run until it settles. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_start/hunt","type":"object"},"label":{"description":"A name to find the job by (scripts, the dashboard).","type":"string"},"mover":{"description":"A pattern on an aperiodic tiling followed far, and stored with its distance when verified. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_start/mover","type":"object"},"pile":{"description":"One large sandpile: N grains dropped on one cell of an unbounded grid. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_start/pile","type":"object"},"resume":{"description":"Carry on this job (stopped, paused, or cut off) instead of starting one.","type":"integer"},"search":{"description":"Soups on a bounded grid of any tiling, aperiodic patches too. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_start/search","type":"object"},"threads":{"description":"Worker threads (default 0: all cores, and all but two for an explore search; results do not depend on them).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"wait_s":{"description":"Wait up to this many seconds for the job to end, then answer with its status (default 0: answer at once).","maximum":600.0,"minimum":0,"type":"number"}},"type":"object"},"name":"search_start","title":"Start or resume a search"},{"annotations":{"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Reports a library job's progress, whatever started it and whatever its kind (hunts, ant searches, piles, movers, collisions, censuses, evolve and explore searches). With `wait_s` (at most 600) it waits for a running job to end before answering, so one call replaces many polls. `finds` adds the job's newest and rarest finds (pattern ids for library_query); `report` gives a Markdown report of what it searched and found instead. Without `job`, lists the jobs, newest first, optionally of one kind or status. Examples: {\"job\": 3, \"wait_s\": 300}, {\"job\": 3, \"finds\": 10}, {\"job\": 3, \"report\": true}, {\"kind\": \"ants\"}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"finds":{"description":"Include this many of its newest and rarest finds (hunts, bounded searches, collisions).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"job":{"description":"The job (default: list the jobs, filtered as job_status).","type":"integer"},"kind":{"description":"Listing: only jobs of this kind.","type":"string"},"label":{"description":"Listing: only jobs with this label.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Listing: at most this many.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"prefix":{"description":"Listing: only jobs whose label starts with this.","type":"string"},"report":{"description":"With `job`: a Markdown report of what it searched, for how long, and what it found.","type":"boolean"},"status":{"description":"Listing: only jobs with this status.","type":"string"},"wait_s":{"description":"Wait up to this many seconds for a running job to stop running before answering (default 0: answer now).","maximum":600.0,"type":"number"}},"type":"object"},"name":"job_status","title":"Job status, finds and report"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Stops a running job at its next checkpoint (a few seconds), in whatever process runs it: here, the command line, a script, or the app. It stays resumable: search_start {\"resume\": job} carries it on (a hunt, ant search, pile, evolve or mover job then ends exactly as an uninterrupted run would; an explore search continues from its archive). Example: {\"job\": 3}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"job":{"description":"The job id.","type":"integer"}},"required":["job"],"type":"object"},"name":"job_stop","title":"Stop a job"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Reads an explore search's stored runs (`job` picks it, default the newest). With no action: its runs, best first, with their measures (fate, settle time, period, density, activity, movers, score: about 0 to 3, higher is more interesting), or to a CSV file. Or one action: `sheet`, a labelled picture of runs at several moments, to judge by eye ({\"sheet\": {\"ids\": [12, 40, 7]}}); `scene`, one run's scene JSON for world_new ({\"scene\": {\"run\": 12}}); `try`, a configuration of your own run now, with its measures and a picture ({\"try\": {\"tiling\": \"hex\", \"rule\": \"B2/S34\", \"seed\": \"random:0.3\"}}); `review`, your verdict on a run ({\"review\": {\"run\": 12, \"verdict\": \"keep\"}}), which feeds what is published and the score; `refit` fits a score model to them, `rescore` applies it. Sealed runs are also Parquet files (runs/part-*.parquet).","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"csv":{"description":"Write them to this CSV file (limit 0: all).","type":"string"},"family":{"description":"Only this rule family (life_like, generations, ltl, jaca, cyclic, ...).","type":"string"},"fate":{"description":"Only runs that ended this way: died, froze, cycle, running.","type":"string"},"ids":{"description":"These runs, instead of the filters.","items":{"type":"integer"},"type":"array"},"job":{"description":"The explore job (default: the newest).","type":"integer"},"limit":{"description":"Most runs to return (default 40, at most 200).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"measures":{"description":"Measures to add: all, or names."},"min_movers":{"description":"Only runs with at least this many moving objects.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"min_score":{"description":"Only runs with at least this score.","type":"number"},"order":{"description":"score (default, best first), newest, or id.","type":"string"},"refit":{"description":"Fit a score model. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_runs/refit","type":"object"},"rescore":{"description":"Rescore a stopped job. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_runs/rescore","type":"object"},"review":{"description":"Record a verdict on a run. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_runs/review","type":"object"},"reviewed":{"description":"Only reviewed runs: any, keep, maybe, or drop.","type":"string"},"scene":{"description":"One run's scene JSON. Needs `run`. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_runs/scene","type":"object"},"sheet":{"description":"A contact sheet of runs, returned as a picture (at most 36 runs). Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_runs/sheet","type":"object"},"stage":{"description":"1 screened (default), 2 confirmation runs on bigger grids.","maximum":255,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"tiling":{"description":"Only this tiling: an id such as hex or k2-017.","type":"string"},"try":{"description":"Try one configuration now (CPU), returning its measures and a picture. Needs `tiling`, `rule`. Settings: jetcarp://schema/search_runs/try","type":"object"}},"type":"object"},"name":"search_runs","title":"An explore search's runs"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Renders media and returns the file paths: per-step PNG frames, an animation (GIF when small, else animated WebP), a poster frame and a thumbnail, in one house style. Give one of `pattern` (alone on an empty field for one seamless period; spaceships in a window that moves with them, guns with their stream), `ant` (a highway's loop in a window moving with the ant, or with mode seed the run from step 0), `quickstart` (from its seed), `scene` (from its seed, into the output folder) or `missing` (every record whose media are missing or stale). Library records' media are stored once by content in the library's media/ folder, and up-to-date media are not rendered again. `poster`: true also returns the first poster inline, to look at. Examples: {\"pattern\": \"glider\", \"poster\": true}, {\"ant\": \"ant-...\", \"mode\": \"seed\", \"gens\": 300}, {\"missing\": true, \"class\": [\"spaceship\"], \"limit\": 20}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ant":{"description":"An ant run (`ant-...`): a highway's moving loop alone, or the build-up from the seed.","type":"string"},"class":{"default":[],"description":"With `missing`: only patterns of these classes (spaceship, oscillator, gun, ...).","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"every":{"description":"From the seed: a frame every this many generations (default 1).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"force":{"default":false,"description":"Render even when up to date.","type":"boolean"},"format":{"description":"auto (default: GIF up to 320x320 pixels and 256 colours, else WebP), gif, or webp.","type":"string"},"frames":{"description":"Write the per-step PNG frames (default true).","type":"boolean"},"gens":{"description":"From the seed: generations (default 200; row rules one per row).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"limit":{"default":0,"description":"With `missing`: at most this many targets (0: no limit).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"missing":{"default":false,"description":"Every pattern, shown Quick Start entry, and notable ant run whose media are missing or stale.","type":"boolean"},"mode":{"description":"auto (default: patterns alone, everything else from the seed), alone, or seed.","type":"string"},"only_patterns":{"default":false,"description":"With `missing`: patterns only.","type":"boolean"},"only_quickstart":{"default":false,"description":"With `missing`: Quick Start entries only.","type":"boolean"},"out":{"description":"With `scene` or a built-in Quick Start entry: the folder for its files (default `<output folder>/media/<scene name>`).","type":"string"},"palette":{"description":"A palette instead of the house style: a built-in name, or hex colours like `#103050-#4fc3ff`.","type":"string"},"pattern":{"description":"A library pattern: id, unique id prefix, or name.","type":"string"},"periods":{"description":"Alone: full periods shown (default 1).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"poster":{"description":"Also return the first target's poster inline (PNG).","type":"boolean"},"quickstart":{"description":"A Quick Start entry: a catalog one (`find:...`, media stored in the catalog) or a built-in one (`life`), rendered from its seed into `out`.","type":"string"},"scene":{"description":"Any scene (JSON: the object or its text), from its seed, into `out` (not the catalog)."}},"type":"object"},"name":"media_render","title":"Render animations and posters"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Packs: signed, content-addressed folders of library records (Parquet tables and JSON) that anyone can read, check and import. Give one action as a key holding its options: `info` (a version's summary), `check` (every hash, id and signature, importing nothing), `import` (into the library, records merged by id), `publish` (the library, or a selection, as a new signed version of a feed in a store), `export` (one version laid out with readable file names, for a single download) or `site` (the website export). Paths must be inside the output folder (relative paths start there), the library's folder, or the packs that came with JETCARP. Publishing signs with the publisher key in JETCARP's settings, which only the user makes (`jetcarp pack key`). Examples: {\"info\": {\"path\": \"packs/starter\"}}, {\"import\": {\"path\": \"packs/starter\"}}, {\"publish\": {\"feed\": \"my-finds\", \"to\": \"packs/my-finds\", \"query\": {\"class\": \"spaceship\"}}}, {\"export\": {\"from\": \"packs/my-finds\", \"to\": \"my-finds-1\"}}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"check":{"description":"Check a store or export without importing it. Needs `path`. Settings: jetcarp://schema/pack/check","type":"object"},"export":{"description":"Lay one version out with readable file names. Needs `to`. Settings: jetcarp://schema/pack/export","type":"object"},"import":{"description":"Import a store or export into the library. Needs `path`. Settings: jetcarp://schema/pack/import","type":"object"},"info":{"description":"A version's summary. Needs `path`. Settings: jetcarp://schema/pack/info","type":"object"},"publish":{"description":"Publish the library (or a selection) as a new signed version of a feed. Needs `feed`, `to`. Settings: jetcarp://schema/pack/publish","type":"object"},"site":{"description":"The website export into the folder `to`. Needs `to`. Settings: jetcarp://schema/pack/site","type":"object"}},"type":"object"},"name":"pack","title":"Packs and the website export"},{"annotations":{"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Lists what JETCARP wrote, read only: the output folder (root \"out\", the default: script runs, sweep folders, piles/, wallpapers/, media of scenes) or the library's folder (root \"catalog\": library.sqlite, media/, search folders). `path` is a folder relative to the root, or an absolute folder from another tool's output (it must be inside a root). Each entry has its name, kind, size, modified time, and for folders what marks them (manifest.json: a sweep or export; pile.json: a pile). `file` returns a small text file (JSON, CSV, text, Markdown, Rhai; the first 64 KB). Examples: {}, {\"path\": \"piles\"}, {\"file\": \"piles/hex-1000000/pile.json\"}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"file":{"description":"A text file inside the root to read instead of listing (json, csv, txt, md, rhai, log, html, tsv; first 64 KB).","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Most entries listed, newest first (default 100, at most 500).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"Folder inside the root, relative or absolute (default: the root itself).","type":"string"},"root":{"description":"Which root: \"out\" (default: the output folder) or \"catalog\" (the catalog's folder).","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"files_list","title":"List output files"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Chooses which world the other tools act on. attach=true: the world in the JETCARP desktop app the user is watching, so they see every change as it happens (the user must first switch it on in the app: Tools, AI control..., Allow AI control; or start the app with `jetcarp --control`. The app then also offers app_display, its displays and screensaver). attach=false: this server's own private world (the default unless the server was started with --app). Returns the attached world's status.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"attach":{"description":"true = act on the app's world, false = the private world. Default true.","type":"boolean"},"port":{"description":"App port, if not the one the app recorded.","maximum":65535,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"token":{"description":"App token shown in its AI control window, if needed.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"use_app","title":"Attach to the JETCARP app"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Controls the JETCARP background host, which runs live scenes as wallpapers or windows without the app. Returns its status (each screen's scene, cell size and caption, and recent problems). Fails if it is not running (`jetcarp host start` starts it).","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"description":"Default status. wallpaper: every screen on the desktop background (GNOME: with the extension) or in a window; login: start at login or not; open_app opens the app; reload rereads host.json; tune sweeps cell sizes on screen (pick: recommended, finest, own or px); scene: a screen's scene.","enum":["status","next","previous","pause","resume","rotation","wallpaper","login","open_app","reload","tune","scene","quit"],"type":"string"},"cpu_limit":{"type":"number"},"fps":{"type":"number"},"gpu_limit":{"type":"number"},"name":{"description":"With rotation: the one to run (saved).","type":"string"},"on":{"description":"With wallpaper, login or tune: on or off. Default on.","type":"boolean"},"pick":{"type":["string","number"]},"screen":{"description":"Counted from 0. Default: every screen for next, previous and tune, else the first.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"}},"type":"object"},"name":"host_control","title":"JETCARP background host"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Reads and changes how the JETCARP app shows the grid. With no arguments it returns the state: where the grid shows (the window, full screen, or outputs: chrome-less full-screen windows on chosen monitors, spanning one canvas or mirroring one view), the monitors (by the index `monitors` takes), the canvas and cell size, running state and speed, the menu and panes, keep-awake, and the screensaver: its mode, rotation and profiles. Arguments change those, several at once, in a sensible order (outputs and cell size before the screensaver starts). Examples: {\"screensaver\": true, \"profile\": \"Hodgepodge\"}, {\"saver\": {\"source\": \"rotation\", \"rotation\": \"Classics, hourly\"}}, {\"mode\": \"outputs\", \"monitors\": [0, 1], \"arrangement\": \"span\"}, {\"cell_px\": 1, \"refill\": true}, {\"skip\": \"next\"}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"arrangement":{"description":"span: one canvas across the outputs by their positions; mirror: the same view on each.","enum":["span","mirror"],"type":"string"},"cell_px":{"description":"Cell size in physical pixels (1 to 64), used by refill and pixel_zoom.","maximum":64,"minimum":1,"type":"number"},"delete_rotation":{"description":"Delete a rotation of yours by name (a built-in's edited copy reverts to the built-in).","type":"string"},"fullscreen":{"description":"Shorthand: true is mode fullscreen, false is mode window.","type":"boolean"},"fullscreen_monitor":{"description":"Monitor index for full screen; null: the monitor the window is on.","type":["integer","null"]},"gpu":{"description":"The app's own GPU choice: follow JETCARP's shared setting, on or off (saved).","enum":["follow","on","off",true,false],"type":["string","boolean"]},"hide_preview":{"description":"With outputs on, draw no grid in the main window (saves GPU work).","type":"boolean"},"identify":{"description":"true: show each monitor's index full screen on it for three seconds.","type":"boolean"},"keep_awake":{"description":"Keep the computer awake (no blanking, locking or suspend) while the app is open.","type":"boolean"},"menu_autohide":{"description":"Auto-hide the menu bar.","type":"boolean"},"mode":{"description":"Where the grid shows: the main window, the main window full screen, or the output windows.","enum":["window","fullscreen","outputs"],"type":"string"},"monitors":{"description":"Output monitors by index (full screen on each). Also sets mode outputs unless mode is given.","items":{"type":"integer"},"type":"array"},"panes_hidden":{"description":"Hide every pane (the grid fills the main window).","type":"boolean"},"pixel_zoom":{"description":"true: zoom so one cell edge is cell_px pixels, the camera snapped to whole pixels.","type":"boolean"},"playing":{"description":"Run (true) or pause (false) generations.","type":"boolean"},"profile":{"description":"A screensaver profile by name (the state's `profiles` lists them; a complete setup): the screensaver shows it from now on, switching to it at once if running.","type":"string"},"refill":{"description":"true: rebuild the tiling now to fill the canvas at cell_px (periodic tilings), zoomed pixel-exact.","type":"boolean"},"rotation":{"description":"A rotation by name (the state's `rotations` lists them): the screensaver runs it from now on, switching to it at once if running.","type":"string"},"save_rotation":{"description":"Create or replace a rotation. Settings: jetcarp://schema/app_display/save_rotation","type":"object"},"saver":{"description":"Screensaver settings to change (saved). Settings: jetcarp://schema/app_display/saver","type":"object"},"screensaver":{"description":"Start (true) or end (false) screensaver mode: no controls, the grid running on the outputs (or full screen).","type":"boolean"},"skip":{"description":"While the screensaver runs a rotation: show the next or previous item now.","enum":["next","previous"],"type":"string"},"speed":{"description":"Generations per second; 0 runs as fast as possible.","minimum":0,"type":"number"},"status_bar":{"description":"Show the status bar.","type":"boolean"},"units":{"description":"Span units: physical pixels, or logical pixels (for monitors of mixed scale factors).","enum":["pixels","logical"],"type":"string"},"windows":{"description":"Outputs as plain windows instead of monitors, each \"WxH@X,Y\" (pixels, at canvas position X,Y), to try spans on one monitor; sets mode outputs unless mode is given.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"type":"object"},"name":"app_display","title":"The app's displays and screensaver"}],"ttlMs":3600000}}
